cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Breaking the Loop: The Reality Audit Framework"
message: "If you use Reality Audit in research, curriculum, or another publication, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Robinson
    given-names: Sandra
    affiliation: "Big Wella"
    website: "https://bigwella.com"
abstract: >-
  Reality Audit is an AI-literacy framework for
  secondary and adult learners and the people who teach them. It names a
  four-stage loop — Intention, Interaction, Response, Reflection — and an
  Academic Branch that verifies learning, giving teachers the practitioner
  moves to keep students the pilot of their own thinking when AI is built to
  agree with them. The framework is grounded in cognitive science (cognitive
  offloading, productive struggle, metacognitive laziness, the illusion of
  mastery), the documented tendency of AI systems toward sycophancy, and
  Australian classroom equity research. The repository contains the full
  Teacher Guide, two assessment rubrics (A–E and four-level), an interactive
  walk-through tool for use alongside a teacher, and a Claude skill file.
keywords:
  - AI literacy
  - generative AI in education
  - AI sycophancy
  - secondary education
  - adult education
  - lifelong learning
  - Australian education
  - metacognition
  - productive struggle
  - cognitive offloading
  - critical thinking
  - assessment
  - teacher professional learning
